At each repetition depth, matched substitutions agree on the
length for the current prefix; no such agreement is required
between different rows. An empty row is therefore not a
missing capture. A single pattern pairing both columns ensures
shape agreement, but length checks become important when a
template combines captures from independent pattern repetitions.
With indexed captures, expansion visits each row and column
once, apart from the costs of constructing and subsequently
expanding the generated syntax.
